  "result": "Perfect! All 149 tests pass. I've successfully implemented the payments system:\n\n**src/payments.js:**\n- `balanceDue(invoice)` - returns the amount still owed\n  - Calculates total from invoiceTotals\n  - Subtracts sum of recorded payments\n  - Clamps at 0\n\n- `recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })` - records a payment on an invoice\n  - Validates status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (NOT_ISSUED error)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Validates date is valid (DATE_INVALID error)\n  - Checks payment doesn't exceed balance due (OVERPAYMENT error)\n  - Creates invoice.payments array if missing\n  - Appends payment to array\n  - Updates status dynamically:\n    - 'paid' if total payments >= invoice total\n    - 'partially_paid' if some payment made but not fully paid\n  - Returns ok(newInvoice) without mutating original\n  - Preserves invoice.number if it exists\n\n**Error codes added:**\n- NOT_ISSUED \u2014 can only record payments on issued or partially_paid invoices\n- OVERPAYMENT \u2014 payment exceeds amount owed\n\n**Tests added (22 new):**\n- balanceDue calculations (unpaid, partially paid, fully paid)\n- recordPayment creates and appends to payments array\n- Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n- Error handling for all invalid inputs\n- Non-mutation of original invoice\n- Preservation of invoice number\n- Multiple payments on same invoice\n- Overpayment detection at different stages\n\nThe system correctly handles partial and full payments, preventing overpayments while allowing multiple payment installments.",
